# Trivy suppression file.
#
# One entry per line. Formats:
#   CVE-2024-12345                       (silence a CVE globally)
#   CVE-2024-12345 exp:2026-01-01        (silence with expiry)
#   AVD-DS-0002                          (silence a misconfig rule id)
#
# Every entry should be justified in a comment. Prefer fixing over ignoring.

# KSV-0109 -- "ConfigMap stores secrets".
#
# Fires on rendered/all.yaml for rhdh-developer-hub-app-config, on the keys
# clientSecret, secret, password and token. Every one of those holds a shell
# placeholder, not a value:
#
#   clientSecret: ${AUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET}
#   secret:       ${BACKEND_SECRET}
#   password:     ${POSTGRESQL_ADMIN_PASSWORD}
#   token:        ${GITHUB_TOKEN}
#
# RHDH expands these at boot from env vars sourced out of Secrets, which is the
# configuration mechanism the product documents -- there is no secret in the
# ConfigMap to move. Trivy matches on key name and cannot see the indirection.
# Re-check if app-config ever gains a key holding a literal.
AVD-KSV-0109

########################################
# Lean EKS profile — terraform/platform
########################################
# The four entries below are consequences of the cost profile this cluster was
# deliberately built to, NOT oversights. They are grouped so the trade is
# reviewed as one decision. Every one of them goes away by moving to private
# subnets + a NAT gateway (~$33/month) and a restricted API endpoint — see
# "Hardening" in terraform/platform/README.md.

# AVD-AWS-0040 / AVD-AWS-0041 -- public EKS endpoint, open to 0.0.0.0/0.
#
# This profile has no NAT gateway, no bastion and no VPN, so there is no
# private path to the API server: a private-only endpoint locks out every
# operator and Terraform itself. It is also load-bearing for CI, because the
# verify job in .github/workflows/platform.yml runs on GitHub-hosted runners
# whose egress addresses are dynamic and cannot be allowlisted.
#
# What keeps this defensible: authentication is IAM via EKS access entries, so
# the endpoint is not an unauthenticated surface. Narrow
# var.public_access_cidrs the moment a stable egress range exists — it is the
# highest-value hardening step available in this profile.
AVD-AWS-0040
AVD-AWS-0041

# AVD-AWS-0164 -- subnets assign public IPs.
#
# Same root cause. With no NAT, nodes need a routable address to pull images
# and reach the control plane. Their security group allows no inbound from the
# internet, so what is exposed is the kubelet's surface, not the workloads'.
AVD-AWS-0164

# AVD-AWS-0104 -- unrestricted egress on the node security group.
#
# Nodes must reach quay.io for the RHDH image, the RHDH chart repository, and
# the regional EKS and EC2 endpoints. Filtering egress that tightly requires a
# VPC endpoint per service, which together cost more per month than this entire
# cluster. Revisit alongside the NAT decision, not before.
AVD-AWS-0104
